From 8d1b4618f0f0883f921cc2c10eeb7136c6a4de6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy1210 <andy1210@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:50:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 068/149] media: qcom: camss: Add the TPG 1.0.2 of SM8350

Titan 580 (SM8350) has its two test pattern generators as separate TPG
1.0.2 blocks (0xac97000, 0xac98000) in front of the CSI receivers. When
the camera top mux (CPAS top + 0x90) selects TPG n, the CSID reading
CSIPHY n gets the generator's packets instead of the PHY's. A TPG 1.0.2
sends one data type on virtual channel 0, with no lane, VC or payload
settings of its own, which makes it a different block from the TPG 2.x
of camss-tpg-gen1.c.

Add its ops (programming as in the vendor driver's cam_top_tpg_ver2.c,
GPL-2.0) to the TPG framework, a second, shared register region for a
TPG (the camera top, mapped without a request), the two SM8350 TPGs on
their PHYs' clocks, and the regions in the binding.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
